```
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ options, maxWidth }) => {
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [filteredOptions, setFilteredOptions] = useState([]);
  const [selectedOption, setSelectedOption] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const filteredOptions = options.filter((option) => {
      return option.toLowerCase().includes(inputValue.toLowerCase());
    });
    setFilteredOptions(filteredOptions);
  }, [options, inputValue]);

  const handleInputChange = (event) => {
    setInputValue(event.target.value);
  };

  const handleOptionSelect = (option) => {
    setSelectedOption(option);
  };

  const renderOptions = () => {
    return filteredOptions.map((option) => (
      <li
        key={option}
        onClick={() => handleOptionSelect(option)}
        style={{
          cursor: 'pointer',
          backgroundColor: selectedOption === option ? '#eee' : 'inherit',
        }}
      >
        {option}
      </li>
    ));
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={inputValue}
        onChange={handleInputChange}
        style={{ maxWidth, width: '100%' }}
      />
      {filteredOptions.length > 0 && (
        <ul
          style={{
            listStyle: 'none',
            padding: 0,
            margin: 0,
            backgroundColor: '#fff',
            border: '1px solid #ddd',
          }}
        >
          {renderOptions()}
        </ul>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Autocomplete;
```
This component takes in two props:

* `options`: an array of options to autocomplete from
* `maxWidth`: the maximum width of the input field

The component uses three state variables:

* `inputValue`: the current value of the input field
* `filteredOptions`: an array of options that match the current input value
* `selectedOption`: the currently selected option

When the `options` array changes, the component filters the options to only include those that match the current `inputValue`. When the `inputValue` changes, the component updates the `filteredOptions` array accordingly.

The component renders a text input field, and when the user types in the field, it populates a list of available options below the input field. When the user clicks on an option, the component updates the `selectedOption` state variable and updates the list to reflect the selection.

